# Logins saved and filled (cavekit-site-data.md R1, T-661): the test login form submitted asks in the card whether to
# remember the login; OK saves it, about:logins lists it, and the next load of the form has the username and the
# password filled with the page's own input events fired. The login is removed at the end from about:logins.
id: site-logins-save
section: Privacy and site data
item: A submitted login form asks whether to remember the login; OK saves it (about:logins lists it) and the page's next load is filled, its input events fired
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true signon.rememberSignons=true signon.autofillForms=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-login.html
kit: cavekit-site-data.md R1
fixture: site-data-clean
wait rect user 30
probe submit '(function(u,p){document.getElementById("user").value=u;document.getElementById("pass").value=p;document.getElementById("note").value="hello jihad";return "filled "+u;})("jihad-tester","s3cret-41")'
tap go
expect dialog present 8
chrome dialog-ok
expect dialog answered 8
wait line 'logins: remembered for http://192.168.1.245:8077' 6
wait text sent "sent jihad-tester" 15
launch http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-login.html
wait text state "user=jihad-tester pass=s3cret-41" 10
expect text-lacks state "events=0"
launch about:logins
wait text logins "jihad-tester" 10
tap 'sel:.login-row[data-user="jihad-tester"] .login-remove'
tap 'sel:.login-row[data-user="jihad-tester"] .login-remove'
wait text logins "No logins are saved" 6
